On Wed, 8 Mar 2006, Alex Joseph Martini wrote:

> I remember seeing somewhere in the CLL a lojban word for ellipsis in
> {lu} quotations, but I can't find it again in the online version or in
> any of the cmavo lists I have.  Does this ring a bell with anyone?


{li'o}, in selma'o UI.  Note that if you use {lu...li'u} quotes, your quoted
text should still be grammatical, even with the omissions.  If that doesn't
work, then you can always use {lo'u...le'u} quotes with a {li'o} inside.
